# Post-deposit brief. A 200 is a rewrite, so the browser URL and its query
# string stay on /phase2. Pages applies redirects even when a file exists,
# so this static rule has to come before the splat or the catch-all wins.
/phase2       /phase2  200

# Same document today: /phase2/ and /phase2.html 308 to /phase2 and keep
# the query string (name, email, company). Without these, the splat below
# would send them to /start. phase2.html is self-contained (inline CSS/JS);
# it does not request any other file on this host.
/phase2/      /phase2  308
/phase2.html  /phase2  308

# Every other path. No query string on the destination, so Pages appends
# the incoming one (gclid, gbraid, wbraid, utm_*, plan, type, has-website,
# nexq_consent, and any other parameter).
/*  https://nexq.co.uk/start  301
